From f4adab1a00d069b7f230a605ab5a9d07b27fa947 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xf gong <gongxiangfeng@sensedeal.ai>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:42:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] agent: wait for non-zero capacity on virtio-mmio block
 devices

On Firecracker (virtio-mmio), the runtime boots the microVM with zero-length placeholder drives (/dev/vdb../dev/vdi with 0 sectors) and attaches container rootfs or volume block devices after boot via PATCH /drives/drive_N. Firecracker updates the virtio-blk config space, injects VIRTIO_MMIO_INT_CONFIG, and returns HTTP 204 before the guest virtio_blk driver finishes updating the device capacity on its workqueue.

Previously, all three DRIVER_BLK_MMIO_TYPE code paths in kata-agent skipped waiting whenever /dev/vdX already existed. Because placeholder nodes exist from boot and Linux set_capacity_and_notify() emits no change uevent for 0 -> N transitions, mount(2) intermittently raced ahead of the guest capacity update and failed with EIO (EXT4-fs: unable to read superblock).

Add wait_for_virtio_blk_mmio_device() to preserve uevent waiting when /dev/vdX is absent and poll /sys/class/block/<devname>/size (bounded by AGENT_CONFIG.hotplug_timeout) until a non-zero sector count is reported before mounting or attaching the device.

Signed-off-by: xf gong <gongxiangfeng@sensedeal.ai>
